* pa-a1-classA-cs: common-source class-A/AB power amplifier.
* Lineage: textbook CS class-A/AB PA, Cripps "RF Power Amplifiers for
* Wireless Communications" lineage. Bench-v1 anchor (the class c1-analogue
* baseline). Structure-only, ZERO component values.
* Structure: single CS NM1; RF choke L1 feeds the drain from VDD (DC feed,
* RF block); output L-match (series L2 + shunt-C C3 to VSS) to a DC-blocked
* VOUT1 (C4). Input DC-blocked (C1). Published in-topology BIAS NETWORK:
* current-mirror reference (R1 -> diode NM2) sets the gate DC through feed
* resistor R2; gate RF-decoupled from the mirror by that series R2.
* Approved 2026-09-14 (bench round 1, "approve all").
C C1 VIN1 n1
NMOS NM1 n2 n1 VSS VSS
L L1 VDD n2
L L2 n2 n3
C C3 n3 VSS
C C4 n3 VOUT1
R R1 VDD n4
NMOS NM2 n4 n4 VSS VSS
R R2 n4 n1
